T*
(Internet programming encompasses the technologies, protocols, and architectural patterns) Tj
T*
(required to construct interactive, distributed software applications accessible via web) Tj
T*
(browsers across the global Internet.) Tj
T*
(* Client-Server Paradigm: The web operates on a distributed request-response model.) Tj
T*
(The Client \(User-Agent / Web Browser\) requests resources; the Server \(e.g. Apache,) Tj
T*
(Nginx, Node.js\) processes business logic and serves documents.) Tj
T*
(* Uniform Resource Identifier \(URI / URL\): Syntax breakdown:) Tj
T*
(scheme://host:port/path?query#fragment \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(https://lpu.in:443/courses?dept=cse#admissions\).) Tj
T*
(* Domain Name System \(DNS\): Resolves human-readable domain names into) Tj
T*
(machine-routable 32-bit IPv4 or 128-bit IPv6 IP addresses through a hierarchical) Tj
T*
(lookup: Local Cache -> Recursive Resolver -> Root Server -> TLD Server ->) Tj
T*
(Authoritative Name Server.) Tj
T*
(* Hypertext Transfer Protocol \(HTTP/HTTPS\): Stateless application-layer protocol) Tj
T*
(operating over TCP/IP \(port 80 for HTTP, port 443 for TLS-encrypted HTTPS\).) Tj
T*
(- HTTP Request Methods: GET \(retrieve data, idempotent, parameters in URL query string\),) Tj
T*
(POST \(submit data in request body, non-idempotent\), PUT \(replace entire resource\), PATCH) Tj
T*
(\(partial resource modification\), DELETE \(remove resource\).) Tj
T*
(- HTTP Response Status Codes: 1xx \(Informational\), 2xx \(Success: 200 OK, 201 Created\),) Tj
T*
(3xx \(Redirection: 301 Moved Permanently, 304 Not Modified\), 4xx \(Client Error: 400 Bad) Tj
T*
(Request, 401 Unauthorized, 404 Not Found\), 5xx \(Server Error: 500 Internal Server Error,) Tj
T*
(503 Service Unavailable\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
